{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat reader-brief.md'","aggregated_output":"# Reading Step 1 theses: one tracked thing, or more (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Read only this brief and `packet.json` beside it. Do not open other files, run commands or model\ncalls.\n\nEach item is a thesis a research step opened: its question, its outcome (what it tracks) and its period. The rule the step was\ngiven: \"A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event.\"\n\nFor each thesis, classify what its **outcome** (with its question and period) tracks:\n- `one`: one quantity for one period, or one event. A reference figure it is compared with (\"measured against the $119 billion\n  cited\"), the event's own negation (\"permitting or continuing to bar\"), or details of the same event (the fine or remedies of a\n  decision) still count as one.\n- `two_periods`: the same quantity or event for two periods, or a date and an alternative date (\"in 2027 or delayed to 2028\").\n- `two_outcomes`: two different quantities or events (a capacity and a price; whether a deal is signed and its amount).\n- `main_and_second`: one main quantity with a second quantity attached (in brackets, \"and the portion of it\", \"and the resulting\").\n- `alternative`: one outcome with an alternative outcome written beside it as part of what is tracked (\"closes (or restructures)\").\n\nReturn one JSON object per thesis, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else:\n`{\"thesis\": \"u1/clean-1\", \"shape\": \"one|two_periods|two_outcomes|main_and_second|alternative\", \"why\": \"one short phrase quoting the words that decide it\"}`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat packet.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat packet.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud partners for their NVIDIA-powered compute infrastructure, and how large is the resulting guarantee/credit exposure?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The outstanding amount of credit support, guarantees or backstop NVIDIA has extended to AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model, disclosed at its next annual report.\",\n  \"period\": \"Next annual report (Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027, likely filed early 2027): the outstanding amount of credit support/guarantees; set by the reason (obligation already undertaken, tracked at the next annual report).\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee/backstop for OpenAI's lease of a large data center in Ohio — and at what amount — large enough to change NVIDIA's credit risk?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA executes (signs) a guarantee or capacity/lease backstop for OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease, and the resulting amount, by the check date.\",\n  \"period\": \"Check date of 31 December 2027 (18 months from the 1 July 2026 item date): whether the guarantee is signed by then; set by the rule for an unsigned obligation (a check date within 18 months of the item).\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI chip platform begin first shipments — the step that brings revenue — before the end of calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether Vera Rubin reaches first shipments (start of revenue) by the end of 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"End of calendar 2026, the date the item supports ('could begin shipping later this year' relative to its 2 July 2026 date).\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Will the combined data center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027, the aggregate AI-infrastructure spend Nvidia projects and on which its GPU demand depends?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditure for calendar 2027, as disclosed in their full-year results.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (the item's 'next year' from its 2026 date), when the four hyperscalers report full-year capex; set by the item, which projects the figure could reach $1 trillion in 2027 up from around $650 billion in 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What will contract prices for AI memory (LPDDR5X, HBM, 3D NAND/DRAM) be through calendar 2026-2027 — the input that now makes up roughly 25-30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack cost?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The level and direction of contract memory (DRAM, NAND, HBM) prices in 2026-2027 and the resulting per-rack memory content cost (about $2 million on the VR200).\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026-2027 memory contract cycles; set by the item's forward cost period (second half of 2026 and beyond).\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Rubin Ultra rack-scale platform — the Kyber NVL144 architecture that houses 144 Rubin Ultra GPUs — reach first shipments in 2027 as originally planned, or slip to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra rack platform reaches first shipments (the step that brings revenue) in 2027 or is delayed to 2028.\",\n  \"period\": \"2028 — the release date SemiAnalysis reports Kyber has been pushed to from an original 2027; the question is settled when Kyber NVL144 / Rubin Ultra first ships (the item supports the original-2027-vs-2028 timing).\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-7\",\n  \"question\": \"What will the outstanding amount of NVIDIA's supply (purchase) commitments to suppliers be at its next annual report — the obligations that lock it into buying capacity and services for its AI systems?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The outstanding supply/purchase commitments disclosed in NVIDIA's next annual report, compared with the $119 billion cited in this item.\",\n  \"period\": \"Next annual report (Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027, likely filed early 2027); set by the reason — an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How much revenue will the big four hyperscalers' in-house AI accelerators (Amazon Trainium, Google TPU, Microsoft Maia, Meta MTIA) generate in calendar 2026 — the combined custom-silicon quantity competing with NVIDIA GPUs, whose customers also fund NVIDIA's data center segment?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined calendar-2026 revenue (or disclosed shipment volume) of the four hyperscalers' in-house AI accelerator programmes, as disclosed in their full-year 2026 results and earnings calls.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, measured at the hyperscalers' full-year 2026 disclosures (early 2027); next/current calendar year set by the item's 6 July 2026 date and by the rule that a shared quantity takes its release date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-9\",\n  \"question\": \"What share of Chinese enterprises' AI accelerator budget will be allocated to domestic (Chinese-made) products versus Nvidia over the 12 months following the July 2026 survey, and will it rise toward the 46% executives indicated from 30% today?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The share of surveyed Chinese enterprise AI accelerator budget going to domestic products — and by implication Nvidia's remaining share — over the 12 months after the July 2026 survey.\",\n  \"period\": \"The 12 months from the Jul 7 2026 Bloomberg Intelligence survey (roughly H2 2026 – H1 2027); set by the survey's 'next 12 months' horizon, checked against a follow-up survey.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-10\",\n  \"question\": \"Will the U.S. government (Congress and/or the FCC) enact legislation or regulation to ban or phase out Chinese-made lidar sensors in U.S. autonomous/robotics systems, which would change the sensor options and cost competitiveness available to NVIDIA's DRIVE Hyperion autonomous-vehicle platform?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether proposed U.S. legislation/regulation to phase out Chinese-made lidar technology in the United States is enacted (and its scope and timing).\",\n  \"period\": \"Pending regulatory/legislative decision — checked at NVIDIA's current fiscal year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027), per the rule that a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Will China's government approve imports of Nvidia's H200 AI chips into China — and roughly how many — enabling Nvidia to begin generating H200 revenue in the country?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether Chinese authorities grant approval for Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek and other firms to import Nvidia H200 chips (potentially a total below 200,000), as reflected in official Chinese government decisions and in Nvidia's disclosed China H200 revenue.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's current fiscal year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027), checked at its next annual report/10-K; set by the rule that a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u1/clean-12\",\n  \"question\": \"Will France's competition authority (Autorité de la concurrence) conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU-market practices by the check date, and will it impose remedies or fines?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The French competition authority's conclusion of its antitrust investigation into alleged anti-competitive practices in the cloud-AI and GPU markets, and any remedies or fines imposed.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's current fiscal year-end (fiscal year ending late January 2027); set by the rule that a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners for NVIDIA-powered capacity, large enough to affect its credit risk, by the 2027-12-31 check date?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The amount of guarantees, credit support or similar contingent exposure NVIDIA discloses for AI cloud partners; zero if none.\",\n  \"period\": \"2027-12-31 check date, within 18 months of the 2026-07-01 item\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform, the product line carrying its data-center value, begin shipping by the end of 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform, confirmed by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement.\",\n  \"period\": \"2026-12-31 check date, based on the item's statement, published 2026-07-02, that Vera Rubin could begin shipping later this year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Will China's government allow NVIDIA to sell its H200 AI chips into mainland China, the world's second-largest chip market, by the check date — i.e. will Beijing lift the block that currently keeps NVIDIA's China share at zero despite U.S. clearance?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"An official Chinese government/regulator decision permitting (or continuing to bar) H200 sales in China, confirmed by an official Chinese announcement or by NVIDIA disclosing H200 China revenue/shipments.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal year-end (FY2027, late January 2027), set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision; the item (published 2026-07-02) gives no date for Beijing's decision.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026, and does their combined spend approach the ~$1 trillion level NVIDIA projects for 2027?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Combined calendar-2026 data-center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers, measured against the ~$650 billion plan reported in the item and NVIDIA's ~$1 trillion projection for 2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026, settled by the hyperscalers' Q4 2026 earnings and capex disclosures (reported early 2027).\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture — the rack system designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — begin shipping by end-2027 as originally scheduled, or has it slipped to 2028 as SemiAnalysis reports?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system (paired with Rubin Ultra), confirmed by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement, occurring in 2027 versus slipping to 2028.\",\n  \"period\": \"2027-12-31 check date — the item (published 2026-07-05) says Kyber was slated to debut with Vera Rubin Ultra in 2027 and has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, so end-2027 discriminates the original schedule from the reported delay.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will NVIDIA's own supply purchase commitments total at its next annual report — the item cites $119 billion in supply commitments, a purchase obligation large enough to bear on its cash and credit risk?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply purchase commitments disclosed at its next annual report, measured against the $119 billion figure reported in this item.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027); the item gives no date, so the date is set by the reason — an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will Amazon, Google, Microsoft and Meta spend in calendar 2026 on custom AI accelerators (such as Trainium, TPU, Maia and MTIA), a measure of how much AI compute demand bypasses NVIDIA's GPUs?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Combined calendar-2026 spending by the big four hyperscalers on custom AI accelerators.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2026; settled by the hyperscalers' Q4 2026 earnings and capex/custom-silicon disclosures reported in early 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What share of Chinese companies' AI-accelerator spending will go to domestic suppliers (e.g. Huawei Ascend and DeepSeek's in-house chips) over the next 12 months, and how much will that displace NVIDIA's China demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The share of Chinese AI-accelerator budgets allocated to domestic suppliers, versus roughly 30% today, as reported in industry surveys/market research and reflected in NVIDIA's disclosed China revenue.\",\n  \"period\": \"12 months from the item (by ~mid-2027), per the item's statement that Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Will France's competition authority reach a conclusion/decision — a fine, behavioral remedies or closure — in its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA's alleged anti-competitive practices in the cloud-AI and GPU markets by NVIDIA's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027)?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The French competition authority's decision concluding its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA, including any fine or behavioral remedies imposed.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027), set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision; the item gives no date for the conclusion, only that it is 'nearing a conclusion'.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u2/clean-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How much new high-bandwidth memory (HBM) capacity will the three main producers (SK Hynix, Micron, Samsung) bring online, and will the HBM shortage keep memory prices at record highs through late 2027 — a supply and input-cost constraint on NVIDIA's GPU shipments?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The state of HBM supply and pricing through late 2027: whether any meaningful new HBM capacity comes online before then, and whether record-high HBM/memory prices persist.\",\n  \"period\": \"Late 2027 (the item, published 2026-07-10, says no new HBM supply arrives before late 2027, keeping the shortage and record prices into 2027); set by the item's forecast, settled by memory-market research and producers' capacity disclosures for 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing / credit-support model, and does it materially raise NVIDIA's contingent obligations and credit risk?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The amount of credit support / backstop commitments NVIDIA reports backing AI cloud partners' compute procurement and the resulting credit-risk exposure.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K), expected early 2027 — set by the reason: a credit-support obligation being undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What will the CPU-to-GPU attach ratio in AI inference workloads be in 2026, as Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan says it is beginning to shift from 1 CPU to 8 GPUs toward 1 CPU to 1 GPU?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The reported CPU:GPU ratio for AI inference workloads in 2026, and whether it has moved materially from 1:8 toward 1:1.\",\n  \"period\": \"2026 calendar year — set because the item reports the shift is beginning as of mid-2026 and gives no specific release date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin next-generation AI chip platform, the product line that carries its data center value, begin shipping by a check date (end of calendar 2026)?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Confirmation that first Vera Rubin shipments have begun, versus slipping into 2027 or later.\",\n  \"period\": \"First shipments by end of calendar 2026 — set by the item: the platform 'could begin shipping later this year' in an article dated 2 July 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How many advanced AI accelerators will Huawei, together with its chipmaking partner SMIC, produce in calendar 2026 (combined Huawei-designed Ascend output: 910B, 910C and the new 950PR line)?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined 2026 output of Huawei-designed AI chips manufactured at SMIC, in units, measured against the contested estimates in circulation (Nvidia's report: SMIC above 700,000 Ascend 910C by end-2026 at a 50,000-per-month run rate and several million 910B in 2027; Commerce Secretary Lutnick: 200,000 advanced chips for 2025; Chris McGuire: 800,000 910C in 2025, 2 million in 2026 and 4 million in 2027 as stress cases).\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item's SMIC capacity figures ('by the end of this year ... 50,000 of these chips per month').\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia actually resume selling H200 AI chips into China by Nvidia's FY2027 year-end — i.e., will Beijing permit Chinese commercial users to buy the chips the U.S. cleared for export in December 2025?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether H200 sales to Chinese customers take place (China data-center revenue returning above zero) versus Beijing keeping Nvidia locked out despite the U.S. approval.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027) — set by the reason: a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-6\",\n  \"question\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2027, and will they approach the roughly $1 trillion level Nvidia projects for next year?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined 2027 data center capex of the big four AI hyperscalers, measured against Nvidia's ~$1 trillion projection and the 2026 level of ~$650 billion.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the item: Nvidia projects hyperscaler capex could reach $1 trillion 'next year' in an article dated 4 July 2026.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture — the rack system that houses its Rubin Ultra generation, the generation after Vera Rubin — reach first shipments in 2028, after SemiAnalysis reported the program has slipped more than 12 months from a planned 2027 debut?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"First shipments of the Kyber NVL144 rack system (Rubin Ultra generation) in 2028 versus the original 2027 schedule, and whether the larger NVL576 multi-rack system ships in volume at all.\",\n  \"period\": \"First shipments by end of calendar 2028 — set by the item: SemiAnalysis says the Kyber NVL144 architecture 'has been delayed to 2028' from a planned 2027 debut alongside Rubin Ultra.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How large will NVIDIA's supply/purchase commitments (its obligations to buy components and locked-in capacity) be at its next annual report, and is the ~$119 billion level cited in this item growing faster than the revenue those commitments support?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply/purchase commitments disclosed at its next annual report, measured against the ~$119 billion cited in this item.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K), expected early 2027 — set by the reason: an obligation already undertaken is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Will the French competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices with an adverse decision, fine or remedy, and by when?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The French competition authority's conclusion of its antitrust probe into Nvidia's alleged anti-competitive conduct in cloud-AI and GPU markets, including the decision date, finding and any fine or remedy imposed.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027) — set because a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end; the item reports the probe is 'nearing a conclusion.'\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How much new high-bandwidth memory (HBM) production capacity will SK Hynix, Micron and Samsung bring online in calendar 2027, and will it arrive early enough to ease the current HBM shortage and record prices that gate NVIDIA's GPU output?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined new HBM capacity the three producers add in 2027 and whether any of it arrives before late 2027, easing the shortage; measured against the item's forecast that no new HBM supply arrives before late 2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the item's forecast that 'None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027,' which places the supply-easing question in 2027.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Will custom ASIC AI accelerators designed by Broadcom and Marvell take a growing share of the big four hyperscalers' AI accelerator spending in calendar 2027, at Nvidia's expense, given their lower cost per gigawatt?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The split of big-four hyperscaler 2027 AI accelerator spending (and of the 19.5 GW of incremental compute capacity projected for 2027) between custom ASIC racks and Nvidia GPU racks, measured against the item's cost-per-gigawatt estimates of $6–11 billion for Broadcom/Marvell ASIC racks versus roughly $19 billion for Nvidia GB300-based racks and $25 billion under Vera Rubin.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the item: Morgan Stanley forecasts the big four will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure 'next year' and add 19.5 GW of capacity, the period in which the ASIC-versus-GPU mix plays out.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"u3/clean-12\",\n  \"question\": \"How far will the US crackdown on advanced AI-chip exports to third countries escalate — will the US Commerce Department go beyond its May 2026 guidance and impose formal licensing requirements or other escalated restrictions on AI-chip shipments to third countries such as Malaysia, Singapore and Japan by Nvidia's FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether the US Commerce Department / Bureau of Industry and Security moves beyond its May 2026 guidance to a binding export-licensing rule or other escalated restriction on AI-chip shipments to third countries, and the resulting constraint on Nvidia's sales to those markets.\",\n  \"period\": \"Nvidia's FY2027 year-end (late January 2027) — set by the reason: a pending regulatory decision is tracked to the current fiscal year-end.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will Nvidia's commitments to suppliers (purchase obligations, primarily memory procurement) be at its next annual report, after rising to $279 billion in the second quarter from $119 billion the prior quarter?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The reported amount of Nvidia's commitments to suppliers / purchase obligations disclosed at its next annual report.\",\n  \"period\": \"Next annual report: Nvidia's Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027 (filed in early 2027); set by the rule that an obligation already undertaken is tracked at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia complete its announced $12.9 billion acquisition of Hugging Face, the open-source AI model repository, by a check date within 18 months of the September 2026 announcement?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Whether Nvidia closes (or abandons/restructures) the announced $12.9 billion purchase of Hugging Face, an acquisition that would absorb cash and add a developer-platform asset.\",\n  \"period\": \"Check date within 18 months of the 2026-09-05 item (by approximately 2028-03-05); the item gives no closing date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will Nvidia have guaranteed or committed in credit support for AI infrastructure projects at its next annual report, after agreeing in August 2026 to provide guarantees of up to $105 billion for a data center project in Ohio?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The reported amount of Nvidia's guarantees / credit support for AI infrastructure projects, including the Ohio data center project, disclosed at its next annual report.\",\n  \"period\": \"Next annual report: Nvidia's Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027 (filed in early 2027); set by the rule that an obligation already undertaken is tracked at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Will the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers approach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, as Nvidia expects?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The top five hyperscalers' combined reported capital expenditures for calendar 2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; checked against the top five hyperscalers' reported 2027 capital expenditures in their quarterly filings and annual reports (early 2028). The item gives the 2027 period.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform, the next-generation system now in production and receiving purchase orders from hyperscalers, account for about 20% of the data center segment's revenue in fiscal Q3 2027, as management guided?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Vera Rubin's share of Nvidia's data center segment revenue in fiscal Q3 2027 (the quarter management guided to roughly 20%).\",\n  \"period\": \"Fiscal Q3 2027 (quarter ending late October 2026), reported around November 2026; the item states management expects about 20% of data center segment revenue in that quarter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Will server DRAM prices jump another 260% in calendar 2026, after rising 64% in the second half of 2025, as the item projects?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in server DRAM prices for calendar 2026 versus the prior period, as measured by industry server DRAM price data.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; checked against server DRAM price reports for 2026 (e.g., TrendForce/DRAMeXchange quarterly updates) after the year or in periodic releases. The item states the 2026 projection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will Nvidia's commitments for future equity investments in AI and infrastructure companies be at its next annual report, after reporting $25 billion of such commitments at the end of fiscal Q2 2027?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The reported amount of Nvidia's commitments for future investments at its next annual report.\",\n  \"period\": \"Next annual report: Nvidia's Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027 (filed in early 2027); set by the rule that an obligation already undertaken is tracked at the next annual report.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Will global high-bandwidth memory (HBM) shipments grow by approximately 50%-60% in calendar 2027, still falling short of demand, as the item projects?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Global HBM shipment growth and whether HBM supply remains short of demand in calendar 2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; checked against HBM shipment data and memory manufacturers' 2027 reports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Will global semiconductor revenue reach roughly $975 billion in calendar 2026, including about $500 billion from AI chip sales, as Deloitte estimates?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Calendar 2026 global semiconductor industry revenue and the AI-chip portion of it, the aggregate that underpins demand for Nvidia's data center products.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; checked against full-year 2026 semiconductor industry revenue data (e.g., SIA/WSTS annual statistics or Gartner/IDC 2026 revenue releases) published in early 2027. The item gives the 2026 period.\"\n },\n {\n  \"thesis\": \"acc/clean-10\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NAND demand generated by Nvidia's CMX (Context Memory Storage) architecture, the storage tier built around its BlueField-4 DPU for long-context and agentic inference, exceed 100 million TB in calendar 2027, up from a projected 35 million TB in 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The volume of NAND demand attributable to Nvidia's CMX architecture in calendar 2027, against the item's projection of more than 100 million TB (from 35 million TB in 2026), and whether memory makers' capacity additions keep pace with it.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 with calendar 2026 as base year; settled when full-year 2027 NAND demand/bit-shipment data for CMX are published (early 2028, e.g. TrendForce releases and memory makers' 2027 reports).\"\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
